      "math_academy_id": "q-60216",
      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "By finding the missing values in the ratio table below, determine which of the following graphs represents the given relationship.\n\n| $x$ | $y$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $2$ | $1$ |\n|  | $3$ |\n| $8$ |  |\n\n$$\n\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "We start with the ratio $2:1$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{1}\n$$\n\nWe can generate equivalent ratios by finding equivalent fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2\\times 3}{1\\times 3} & =\\frac{6}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2\\times 4}{1\\times 4} & =\\frac{8}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our ratio table:\n\n| $x$ | $y$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $2$ | $1$ |\n| $6$ | $3$ |\n| $8$ | $4$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following ordered pairs: $(2,1),$ $(6,3),$ $(8,4).$\n\nPlotting these points on the coordinate plane, we get:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14152648/assets/67a63fc01a35a6f1a91153e25383b84d8b320c6c09eab2194ee39cd570ed799f.png)",
